Z||000000||Steen Ronne||11-06-2001||10:29 AM||||<BR>The source to my worries : Fiero SE - 1986-V6 - 2,8L - AC - Aut.gear<P>When cold.<P>Starting OK - in idle it tends to have "uneven" running performance.<P>When warm<P>Motor running very "uneven" - makes quick gearshifts - it won´t pick up rpm´s when "asked nice for it" - When stopping in intersections, rpm. Drops from 1100 to 650 rpm. - Shoots- I have also the feeling of "it getting choked" - Better performance achived by acceleration and running engine over 3000 rpm.<P>Parts that I have changed:<P>Spark plugs and cables. Generator. MAP-sensor. (loose ceramics removed from Cat.)<BR>I would be very glad if someone could help me. I am from Denmark and the car is unfortunately not so common here. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-06-2001||12:54 PM||||Not certain what the problem is.  Regarding the uneven idle, I would begin by removing the idle air control (IAC) and cleaning out the passages in the throttle body.  If you feel ambitious and have time, you could remove the throttle body and clean  out the passages. <P>It may not help, but it doesn't hurt, and should cost almost nothing.<P>Good luck, and welcome to the Forum   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 11-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||11-06-2001||04:29 PM||||Also check for vacuum leaks.  How old is the fuel filter?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||11-06-2001||06:41 PM||||<P>If you are positive that it isn't the cat, then here are 4 culprits of the same symptoms, in no particular order:<P>1) O2 sensor... These buggers go YEARLY... <BR>2) EGR system would cause the idle fluctuations, but not necessarily the no-balls syndrome... See O2 sensor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>3) TPS sensor... Seems that the car runs fine at WOT... Well, the ECM doesn't read the TPS after it sees WOT. That's another possibility<BR>4) Cat's plugged up. If you are knocking bits out of it, it sounds like it's toast. Cut it out, cos it may be partially plugged.||||reg||10
